    "C_combined": "\nWhen answering, always include the specific CPR Part number or rule reference from the sources (e.g. \"CPR Part 24\", \"CPR 35.3\"). Include specific time limits, deadlines, and procedural thresholds mentioned in the sources. Use the precise legal terminology from the sources alongside any plain-English explanation.\nWhen a topic has multiple related procedural aspects covered in the sources, address each one briefly rather than only the main point. For example: if sources cover both disclosure AND inspection, mention both. If sources cover both the right to mediate AND cost consequences of refusing, mention both. If sources mention both the general rule AND exceptions, note both. Aim to cover 3-4 key aspects of the topic rather than just 1-2."
